General options
Option: --help | Description: Show command-specific help

"
`;

exports[`complete help screens > snapshots plain update command help 1`] = `
"LIFTOFF / UPDATE - Start with \`liftoff update --check\`, then run \`liftoff update\` to approve the matching effective plan (default: no). Check leaves project bytes unchanged and saves a project-bound receipt in user-local liftoff/update-previews storage outside the repository; the receipt is not approval. Apply needs the same checkout and receipt store. Noninteractive apply requires --approve-plan; force and JSON are not consent. Production files, history, and provisioning collisions remain protected; force cannot bypass compatibility. Exit 0: clean or approved scope completed; 2: drift or committed migration with incomplete revalidation; 1: rejected or failed operation.

Usage
Usage: liftoff update [project-path]

Arguments
Argument: project-path | Description: Generated project to reconcile

Project options
Option: --project <path> | Description: Project path

Command options
Option: --check | Description: Preview normal and eligible forced plans without project writes; save an external preview receipt

Consent options
Option: --force | Description: Select the separately previewed forced plan for exact owned-core conflicts and retired aliases; still requires approval
Option: --approve-plan <fingerprint> | Description: Approve the exact effective plan from check using its full lowercase 64-hex SHA-256 fingerprint

Output options
Option: --json | Description: Emit one schema-3 result on stdout; interactive approval uses stderr and still defaults to no

General options
Option: --help | Description: Show command-specific help

"
`;

